.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt WISP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wisp
.Nd local-first differential OKF knowledge store
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm wisp
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
stores an Open Knowledge Format (OKF) bundle as an append-only, section-level
changeset log with encrypted cold payloads and a hot SQLite tier.
The ledger is authoritative; managed markdown on disk is a cache refreshed
asynchronously after headless commits unless a barrier runs.
.Pp
Every command accepts
.Fl -json
and prints one JSON envelope on stdout.
Exit codes are stable: 3 conflict, 4 refused, 5 validation, 7 retryable busy,
8 integrity, 9 key unavailable, 10 erase pending.
.Pp
Agent fleets: see
.Pa docs/AGENT-WRITERS.md
in the source tree (hot reads, exit 3, append vs update, materialize barriers).
.Sh REPOSITORY
Discover the nearest ancestor directory containing
.Pa .wisp/
or pass
.Fl -repo .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss Repository lifecycle
.Bl -tag -width 12n
.It Cm init
Create
.Pa .wisp/ ,
default policies, and ref
.Va main .
.It Cm import
Adopt a directory or
.Fl -git
repository.
.It Cm status
Changed, new, missing, and non-conformant files; pending erasures;
materialize backlog in JSON
.Pq Fl -json .
.It Cm materialize
Flush the async worktree materialize queue.
.Fl -wait
blocks until pending publish jobs for managed checkouts finish.
Use before tools that read bundle paths without using hot APIs.
.It Cm record
Commit working-tree edits as one changeset; drains materialize before return.
.Fl -resolve
clears
.Pa .wisp/merge.json
after a successful record during merge resolution (not exit-3 retry).
.It Cm checkout , Cm switch
Render a ref to the working tree or
.Fl -to .
.It Cm fsck , Cm gc , Cm backup , Cm restore-backup
Integrity, cache maintenance, and snapshots.
.El
.Ss Headless writes
Commit directly to a ref without requiring disk to match hot first.
.Bl -tag -width 14n
.It Cm update Ar path#section
Replace a section body; requires
.Fl -base
section change id unless
.Va any .
.It Cm add-section , Cm remove-section , Cm set , Cm unset , Cm create
Section and frontmatter operations (see
.Fl -help
per command).
.It Cm apply
Read one JSON batch from a file or stdin and commit as one changeset.
Batch ops include
.Va update_section ,
.Va append_section ,
and
.Va prepend_section
(fragment stitched on hot without a section-version precondition).
See
.Pa docs/APPLY.md .
.It Cm apply Fl -resolve
On
.Va section_conflict
.Pq exit 3 ,
refresh
.Va base_version
from hot and retry until success or the attempt budget is exhausted.
JSON result includes a
.Va resolve
stats object.
.El
.Pp
After
.Cm apply
without
.Fl -resolve ,
call
.Cm materialize Fl -wait
or read via
.Cm cat
and search APIs.
.Sh READ AND QUERY
.Cm cat ,
.Cm log ,
.Cm show ,
.Cm why ,
.Cm impact ,
.Cm diff ,
.Cm search ,
.Cm pack ,
.Cm tokens .
.Sh BRANCHES AND MERGE
.Cm branch ,
.Cm switch ,
.Cm merge ,
.Cm worktree ,
.Cm mv .
Ref merge conflicts use
.Cm merge Fl -resolutions ;
section optimistic conflicts use exit 3 or
.Cm apply Fl -resolve .
.Sh SYNC AND EXPORT
.Cm remote ,
.Cm push ,
.Cm pull ,
.Cm serve ,
.Cm export ,
.Cm import .
.Sh ERASURE
.Cm erase ,
.Cm retract ,
.Cm restore ,
.Cm lifecycle .
Managed checkouts rewrite after shred; unrecorded edits block erase unless
.Fl -discard .
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Cm config
reads and writes
.Pa .wisp/manifest.toml
keys including
.Va commit.busy_timeout_ms ,
.Va commit.retries ,
.Va materialize.enabled ,
and
.Va materialize.tick_ms .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width 14n
.It Ev WISP_ACTOR
Default actor when
.Fl -actor
is omitted.
.It Ev WISP_MASTER_KEY
64-hex keystore unlock for CI and automation.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Pa .wisp/manifest.toml
.Pa .wisp/ledger.db
.Pa .wisp/payloads/
.Pa .wisp/keys/
.Pa .wisp/cache/refs/
.Pa hot.db
(rebuildable)
.Pa .wisp/checkout.idx
(primary tree index)
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Pa docs/WORKTREE.md
async materialize,
.Pa docs/APPLY.md
batch format,
.Pa docs/MERGE.md
ref merge,
.Pa docs/ERASE.md
erasure,
.Pa docs/CONCURRENCY.md
writers and exit codes.
.Sh INSTALL
Copy this file to
.Pa share/man/man1/wisp.1
.Pq or
.Pa ~/.local/share/man/man1/wisp.1
when installing the
.Nm
binary.
